From cf88fd9c901f645163bd68c11c4d05d6d046bcd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c-drew <101952850+c-drew@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:13:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] Fixed render scale for DLSS-RR, fork settings file,
 frame timing tools

Render scale: every render-resolution image keeps the DLSS mode's size and a frame renders
into its top-left sub-rectangle, which DLSS-RR is told about. MCVR_RENDER_SCALE (per axis,
relative to the mode's size) picks a size between the DLSS presets, e.g. 0.78125 of Quality
at 1440p = 1333x750. Passes that read image sizes use WorldUBO.renderSizePacked instead;
temporal passes reproject with the previous frame's size. A dynamic controller (MCVR_DRS=1)
exists but is off: DLSS-RR spends ~14 ms of CPU on every render size change.

Settings: mcvr_fork::setting() reads the environment variable, else the same key from
<game dir>/radiance/fork.properties, so a launcher-started game keeps its settings.

Timing: MCVR_TIMING_FILE / MCVR_TIMING_FRAMES write per-pass GPU timestamps,
MCVR_CPU_FRAME_LOG writes per-frame render-thread checkpoints and profiler zones.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
